## 1. `campaigns/active/` is not really an “active” portfolio yet

There are 25 files covering Automower, balcony/window hardware, cabin water, Cinderella, fire alarm, Flexit, garage doors, Harvia, heat-pump electronics, Helios, hot tubs, HVAC, Ireland heat pumps, marine electronics/pumps, Nilan, Ouman, pipe inspection, pools, radon, recliners, EV chargers, Vallox and Wallas.

But the import commit reveals that these originally came in mostly as **competitor-gap notes**, not fully validated campaigns.  Most subsequently got expanded with generic scaffolding such as:

* “See original campaign file”
* generic 25–35% margins
* “OEM direct if available”
* generic 75-SKU targets
* generic Shopping/Search budgets

without resolving the hard gates.

Even the richer Vallox campaign contains illustrative-looking SKU/MPN/stock/price values that aren't evidence-bound.

So I would change the repo semantics immediately:

```text
campaigns/candidates/
campaigns/blocked/
campaigns/eligible/
campaigns/benchmark/
campaigns/rerouted/
campaigns/live/
```

`ACTIVE` should mean:

> **CG eligibility receipt exists + supplier route exists + actual launch subgraph exists.**

Not “this idea looked good.”

Also: **Allaway is absent from this current active directory**, despite being one of the strongest things we found, while weaker things like Automower, pipe inspection and heat-pump electronics remain active. AKVA is also outside this campaign structure. The portfolio index has therefore drifted from the actual research conclusions.

