# 3. `voiceagent` is already the start of the runtime

This repo is significantly more useful than a standalone voice agent.

It already defines:

```text
PRODUCT → compatible_with → ASSET
PART → supersedes → PART
CUSTOMER → owns → ASSET
ORDER → contains → PRODUCT
```

and explicitly says authoritative facts should remain in graph/tool evidence rather than the LLM.

It already has:

* graph-grounded chat;
* swappable business YAML;
* `IDENTIFY → COMPATIBILITY → REPLACE → BOOK`;
* Norwegian-language handling;
* Shopify-oriented config;
* subgraph merge/import functions;
* voice as an adapter instead of the core.

And its architecture document already says the right thing:

> graph authoritative, LLM not authoritative; public and privileged tool planes separated; voice is an adapter; provenance needs adding.

So I would **not build another commerce-agent repo**.

I would evolve `voiceagent` into:

> **Drop Resolver Runtime**

Voice becomes one channel.

Web chat another.

Product finder another.

Shopify PDP another.

Google another.

ChatGPT/Shopify Catalog another.

