# 4. But change the graph model before adding more campaigns

The current implementation is deliberately tiny: lexical token matching followed by neighbor expansion.

Fine for the MVP.

But this:

```yaml
relation: compatible_with
```

is nowhere near sufficient.

The canonical graph needs explicit typed entities:

```text
OEM
ASSET_FAMILY
MODEL
GENERATION
SERIAL_COHORT
COMPONENT
PART
SKU
SUPPLIER
DOCUMENT
QUESTION
SERVICE
```

and edges like:

```text
HAS_GENERATION
HAS_COMPONENT
FITS
DOES_NOT_FIT
SUPERSEDES
REPLACED_BY
REQUIRES_PART
REQUIRES_ADAPTER
REQUIRES_INSTALLER
EQUIVALENT_TO
SOLD_BY
IN_STOCK_AT
DOCUMENTED_BY
IDENTIFIED_BY
```

Every decisive edge:

```json
{
  "edge_id": "EDGE-GU-00192",
  "from": "GU_OLD_GEARBOX_1994",
  "relation": "REPLACED_BY",
  "to": "GU_NEW_GEARBOX_934K",
  "qualifiers": {
    "backset_mm": 35,
    "centres_mm": 92,
    "spindle_mm": 8
  },
  "evidence": [
    "EV-OEM-PDF-182"
  ],
  "status": "VERIFIED"
}
```

And crucially:

```text
PHOTO SIMILARITY
        ↓
candidate retrieval only

model / serial / measurements / identifiers
        ↓
deterministic compatibility verification
```

The existing Shopify demo config already has the right safety doctrine: don't assert compatibility from visual similarity alone.

