# 11. Google is even better suited to our compatibility thesis

Google now explicitly describes these fields as helping AI systems understand product nuance.

### `product_detail`

Supports up to **100 structured technical details** and Google says it can improve matching to individual product queries, including AI Mode. ([Google Help][8])

For balcony hardware:

```text
Identification:OEM marking:GU
Compatibility:Backset:35 mm
Compatibility:Centres:92 mm
Compatibility:Spindle:8 mm
Compatibility:Handing:Reversible
Compatibility:Door generation:1994–2001
Installation:Skill level:DIY intermediate
Dimensions:Strip length:1800 mm
```

Fantastic.

### `related_product`

Up to 30 relationships, including:

```text
required_part
substitute
accessory
often_bought_with
different_brand
part_of_set
```

and Google says it is primarily intended for conversational experiences such as AI Mode. ([Google Help][9])

However, major correction:

> `related_product` only points to another product by **your Merchant Center product ID or GTIN**.

It cannot represent:

```text
1998 Uldal door
→ fits
→ GU gearbox
```

unless you actually sell the door as a product.

So GMC is **not our entire compatibility graph**.

It expresses the commerce projection of it.

Our full graph stays upstream.

